{"label": "5e38ec62aa36eae80132", "speaker_changes_inside": "no", "view": "own_sincere", "referents": [{"word": "that", "refers_to": "the preceding claim that Bitcoin only has to stay decentralized and secure", "inside": true, "changes_assertion": "no"}], "conditions": [{"text": "all it has to do is stay decentralized and secure", "inside": true}], "retraction": "none", "time_ok": "yes", "proposition": "Bitcoin is a new system of measure for the first free market, and as long as it stays decentralized and secure, that is what emerges regardless of the existing fiat system.", "certainty": "certain", "speaker_is": "guest", "speaker_evidence": "And why that's interesting for this conversation to your initial question is how could we superimpose those two thoughts on what's going on right now?"},
{"label": "316f66f81603ea55899a", "speaker_changes_inside": "no", "view": "own_sincere", "referents": [{"word": "it", "refers_to": "Bitcoin", "inside": true, "changes_assertion": "no"}], "conditions": [{"text": "if the price of Bitcoin goes higher", "inside": true}], "retraction": "none", "time_ok": "yes", "proposition": "A higher Bitcoin price makes Bitcoin better collateral for issuing more dollar credit, and this loop is sustainable because Bitcoin is perfectly scarce while the dollar is not.", "certainty": "likely", "speaker_is": "guest", "speaker_evidence": "Or like, what do you, what do you, is there a specific like point of why you think that would happen?"},
{"label": "5d5e163125435e85061a", "speaker_changes_inside": "no", "view": "own_sincere", "referents": [], "conditions": [{"text": "if you want to have confidence that any purchases of Bitcoin are going to be legal", "inside": true}], "retraction": "none", "time_ok": "yes", "proposition": "To have confidence that administration purchases of Bitcoin are legal, authorization from Congress, which controls the purse strings, would be needed.", "certainty": "certain", "speaker_is": "guest", "speaker_evidence": "So by that, you mean an executive order is not robust enough on its own. This needs to be in law in some way. Yes."},
{"label": "0c751a33022013fb3086", "speaker_changes_inside": "no", "view": "own_sincere", "referents": [{"word": "it", "refers_to": "Bitcoin / the asset", "inside": true, "changes_assertion": "no"}], "conditions": [], "retraction": "none", "time_ok": "yes", "proposition": "In Bitcoin, everyone loves the asset in bull markets and hates it in bear markets, which is itself why the price gets high at the top and low at the bottom.", "certainty": "certain", "speaker_is": "guest", "speaker_evidence": "Yeah, I think situation has changed. And that's... Yeah, that's driven some of these different decisions that we've seen."},
{"label": "9a9ed680fa64a4ae7305", "speaker_changes_inside": "no", "view": "own_sincere", "referents": [], "conditions": [], "retraction": "none", "time_ok": "yes", "proposition": "It is now possible to use Bitcoin completely privately, via one-to-one pegged e-cash, together with private communications.", "certainty": "certain", "speaker_is": "guest", "speaker_evidence": "I mean, you paint such a positive picture of the adoption, but I know a lot of folks out there just wonder, what is this transition going to look like?"},
{"label": "c8827879545a98fdec4e", "speaker_changes_inside": "no", "view": "own_sincere", "referents": [], "conditions": [], "retraction": "none", "time_ok": "yes", "proposition": "Bitcoin functions like a global productivity index, analogous to how the S&P 500 relates to individual stocks, and will likely outperform them.", "certainty": "likely", "speaker_is": "guest", "speaker_evidence": "So how do you see that? Like if you compare Bitcoin versus asset classes or Bitcoin versus individual stocks?"},
{"label": "f81db985a39acf8dcc8e", "speaker_changes_inside": "no", "view": "hypothetical", "referents": [{"word": "it", "refers_to": "whether the bull market would have been higher without treasury companies", "inside": true, "changes_assertion": "no"}], "conditions": [{"text": "if the treasury companies didn't exist (in the past cycle)", "inside": true}], "retraction": "none", "time_ok": "yes", "proposition": "In the past cycle, if treasury companies had not existed, the Bitcoin bull market might have been higher, though it is hard to tell.", "certainty": "speculative", "speaker_is": "guest", "speaker_evidence": "Yeah. And so in some sense, like, sure, like if you were buying a stock. at 10x MNAV back in 2025"},
{"label": "98148a8112d2b2a996d6", "speaker_changes_inside": "no", "view": "attributed", "referents": [{"word": "that", "refers_to": "the study by Sam Callahan and Lyn Alden", "inside": true, "changes_assertion": "no"}, {"word": "it", "refers_to": "that Bitcoin is the single most sensitive asset to money printing", "inside": true, "changes_assertion": "no"}], "conditions": [], "retraction": "none", "time_ok": "yes", "proposition": "A study by Sam Callahan and Lyn Alden shows Bitcoin is the single most sensitive asset to money printing, though that past relationship need not hold in the future.", "certainty": "likely", "speaker_is": "host", "speaker_evidence": "I agree with Pomp, and I think this is an incredible entry point. On the daily chart, Bitcoin is the most oversold since the bottom near 58K."}
]}
